%description:

Tcp.urgentOutOfBand:oob -- the application receives 4343 of the 4344 bytes.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "true: as Linux without SO_OOBINLINE, the last byte of received urgent data
leaves the stream ...; INET does not deliver that byte".

The classes: inline (false, the default) and oob (true, the value of LinuxTcp). The code: with
true, TcpConnection::processUrgentPointer() marks the last urgent byte, at the sequence number
of the segment plus the urgent pointer, less one, and TcpConnection::extractDataForApp() takes
that byte out of the stream; with false, the receiver ignores the urgent pointer. This test separates "oob" from the other value.

Host under test: host2, whose application reads at once; host1 sends 4344 bytes, and the tap
sets the URG bit and an urgent pointer of 100 in the first data segment. Observation: the application of host2 receives 4343 bytes.

%# parameter: Tcp.urgentOutOfBand
%# class: oob
%# value: true
%# key: *.host2.tcp.urgentOutOfBand
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpUrgentOutOfBandOob")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1)
                     .set("tcp.urgBit", "true").set("tcp.urgentPointer", "100")
                     .describe("the first data segment of host1: urgent data up to its 100th byte"))
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host2.app[0]").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                                        .captureSum("received", "length")
                                        .within(2.0)))
        .act(action().at(1.5)
                 .describe("the bytes that the application of host2 received")
                 .assertModule("host2.app[0]", "{received} == 4343B"));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpUrgentOutOfBandOob compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.urgentOutOfBand = true    # the parameter under test
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 4344B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpUrgentOutOfBandOob: PASS
